The clause is clear but doesn't answer the question: "Have any texts been reviewed for compliance?".  It was written two year ago (going by the date on the page) so beginners may reasonably assume that the committee is in existence and doing its job.  Furthermore, the clause is buried deep in the Official Baseline Statement page which is not likely to be seen by the beginner before he looks at the texts.  Note: the Texts In Lojban folder is right there in the main menu on the left.

Why not put a clarifier on top of  http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Texts+In+Lojban&bl.  Something like:

"The following texts have been submitted by members of the lojban community on a best-effort basis.  They may or may not contain errors.  If on reading them, you think you have found an error, please use the a forum for the purposes of reporting and discussing.

The LLG plans to create a committee some time in the future to review submitted texts for compliance .  For more information see the Baseline Compliance section in http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Official+Baseline+Statement&bl "

